================================================================================
Data Files and Their Sources
================================================================================

The MIT License in LICENSE covers the source code of this repository and its
documentation. It does not cover the data files listed below, nor any other
file of this repository that reproduces records from the sources below, such
as exported API responses and test fixtures. Those records remain subject to
their publishers' terms, described in this section.

This section lists the third-party sources that have records in the data
files of this repository, and the terms each publisher attaches to them. It
describes the files as they stand in this revision. Row counts were read on
24 September 2026 at commit 5094d72a; they change at every refresh (monthly
for the BIC data, weekly for the sanctions data). On 25 September 2026 the
records of group C were removed from these files. This section is not legal
advice: where a publisher's terms have not been established, it says so.

Files concerned:
  data/bic.sqlite
  data/compliance.sqlite
  frontend/data/registers/*.json (Germany, Switzerland, Slovakia and Italy),
    frontend/data/countries.json and
    frontend/app/[locale]/playground/captured-iban.json (API responses
    exported for the website; they repeat records from the sources below)
  src/db/bic_data.json (composite map from national bank codes to BICs)
  src/db/nl-psp.json
  scripts/data/eu-emi-register-2026-05-22.json
  scripts/data/iban-registry-2026-05-22.json
  test fixtures and sample API responses elsewhere that repeat these records

Earlier commits of this repository, and forks of it, keep copies of these
files. The data in those copies remains subject to its publishers' terms.

Each source is listed in one of three groups:
  A. terms that permit reproduction, under the conditions stated;
  B. terms not yet confirmed;
  C. not redistributable here, and removed from the files of this
     repository on 25 September 2026; the IBANforge API serves the database
     records among them from a private repository.

